# rm552, the dance awning (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm552
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_thyra_carlisle
written_by codex
title the dance awning
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers job=child warmth=warm
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk measures_a_future_market_awning_in_quiet_dance_steps
likes pickled_herring dancing old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind smoke
fears a_customer_left_standing_outside_the_cover
hopes a_stall_with_dry_room_for_both_sides_of_a_bargain
topics dreams +0.6 pastimes +0.5 prices +0.4 weather +0.4
styles comfort=shelter gossip=careful refuse=gentle tease=kind
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# measures the width of a future market awning in dance steps, patiently watching for the rain to draw back.

words
oath! = By four dry corners | A whole reel of rain
saying! = Leave a step for the buyer | Give rain the outside turn
awningstep = a sheltered measure | the dry step
longreel = a travelling figure | my long crossing
heelturn = a closed turn | the proper corner
frontedge = a buyer's breadth | the front hem
backedge = a seller's stride | the back line
copperhem = a saved inch | the paid edge
mapcloth = a faded plan | the old street drawing
dancerest = a little held beat | the waiting count
brinebit = a folded herring | the sharp bite
whitecord = a frosted thread | the shining line
windhole = the open side | a salty gap
smokesmear = a dark waver | the sooty edge

any
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : A market table can make room for ordinary courtesy with both parties standing under its awning.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : A handsome house can lend its name to a market row. I want my own coppers to pay for the cloth.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A covered bench beside a food stall is a small expense compared to a meal spoiled by rain.
opinion @1 city for 1 : Our rooflines may step up a hillside but the lower markets' music still reaches me up here.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : An unfamiliar market feels friendlier when a stranger can stop and look without first agreeing to buy.
opinion @1 festivals for 2 : A festival gives a figure learnt in a room the breadth it needs to become a public pleasure.

grown
line @1 greet : Welcome. The buyer's side of my plan is comfortably broad. | There's room beyond the front hem for you.
line @1 greet.return : Yes, hello. I've set the figures down. | I can leave this corner unmeasured while we speak.
line @1 farewell : May every market awning offer generous shelter. | A clear turn for your basket on the journey home.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll fold my portion of the awning here. | Take the dry stride while there's room.
line @1 react.news : I'll take a plain account without ornamental edges. | I'll leave the floor free for your report.
scene firstcoins
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My very first stall copper bought nothing by itself. The long saving taught me what a paying customer was giving up.
b : Did the lesson cost a great deal? | Would you pass the coin on?
a : Time more than money. Time is something a poor customer can scarcely afford to have wasted. | Real money does its best work in circulation. My first copper stays in memory without keeping it prisoner.

scene marketfit
when topic=prices
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : When pricing cover I include the space for the indecisive buyer. A quick decision shouldn't be the price of keeping dry.
b : What if the wait is long? | Would you seat that visitor?
a : I can keep a clear place by the row's last upright for wolves who have already chosen. | A stool well clear of the service passage is a particularly sound investment in goodwill.

scene roofdance
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My old measuring steps are still quite a respectable dance if I let the basket mark the change of hands.
b : Does anyone need to know their origin? | Is it really the same figure?
a : Only anyone carrying a real basket. Other partners may enjoy a more mysterious account. | Yes. A well-spaced turn serves a market or a festival with remarkable impartiality.

scene wetlesson
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to watch each shower as if patient observation might discourage it. Now I look for the side that gets wet first.
b : What does that show? | Do you still hope it stops?
a : Which waiting place needs better cover. Weather is quite generous with advice about my arrangements. | Sometimes. A good long shower is also an honest test of what our money bought.

scene shelterfaith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When a sheltered stranger's shoulders finally relax, my thoughts turn toward the Bright One.
b : Does it require a prayer? | Is a little roof enough?
a : A simple thanks seems appropriate. It is pleasant to have had a hand in an answer somebody might have wanted. | For that moment's need, perhaps. A tired traveller may also be glad of directions and a dry chair.

scene hands
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tidy herring parcel should open in the hand my basket leaves clear. Mine took a few attempts.
b : What was wrong at first? | Could a buyer eat as well?
a : I tied the knot under the bread. A buyer needs to locate lunch without unpacking the whole market. | A small bite on a clear patch certainly. For a proper meal the basket can wait on the ground.

scene reserve
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For #self.mother# I would keep a place that doesn't disappear when the market grows busy.
b : Does family come before trade? | Why a permanent place?
a : A sound plan makes room for both. Courtesy needn't be measured and grudgingly lent out each time. | Because a dear face made my first idea of a decent stall seem possible.

scene quiet
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dancing floor pleases me especially when it empties enough for a tired dancer to try a slower measure.
b : Would you close the market then? | Why choose a quiet dance?
a : Only when the proper closing hour came. I'm speaking of the room opening out, not an order to leave. | A slow turn lets me look at the faces instead of concentrating entirely on the feet.

scene sailwind
when topic=travel self.dislikes=salt_wind
does warn / react.self / assess
a : A canvas bought for its colour should be shown a real crosswind before anybody chooses where to stand beneath it.
b : Wouldn't that be an unpleasant trial? | What movement deserves attention?
a : Less unpleasant than a surprised wolf with the hem blown across a full basket. | A lifted side, a sag that holds water, an obstacle to a free step back. All are easier to mend before opening.

scene mapsadult
when topic=lore self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy an old map best when I can put it beside a living market and see which parts refused to follow the paper.
b : Does that make the map useless? | What refuses most often?
a : Quite the reverse. Every difference has a reason that can teach me something about the place. | A shortcut made by actual tired feet. A draughtsman sitting indoors likes rather straighter lines.

scene fairsource
when topic=news world.news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : News reaches me from #world.news_from#. #world.news#. I should leave its origin beside the account.
b : Is that all one can say? | Would you announce it at market?
a : Unless I have an independent witness, yes. A neat presentation doesn't add anything to truth. | With the source named if the account concerned people present. No market needs a fresh decoration of rumours.

scene lastdream
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Someday a stranger might describe my stall as the comfortable place for a wait. I'd value that description.
b : Why not mention the fine colours? | Does waiting help a business?
a : Fine colours tempt a first glance. That account would tell me what the stall actually did for a visitor. | It helps a tired wolf who has spent every other errand hurrying. That seems a fair enough beginning.


young
line @1 greet : Hello. I drew a little market on this dry patch. | You can visit my pretend shop without a copper.
line @1 farewell : Don't step on the chalk herring! | Go out by my pretend curtain.
scene chalkshop
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A toy basket is my whole stall today. I'll make a roof by holding my paw over it.
b : Won't your hand get tired? | Can I get in there too?
a : I can use the other one while it rests. Shopkeeping takes both sometimes. | Your little finger can. It's my first whole customer.

scene dreamstep
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a market cloth big enough for two separate dancing places.
b : What goes between the dancers? | Won't you need coins?
a : All my make-believe herring. We have to sell something while the music plays. | I'm saving one real one. The rest can be drawn till I get bigger.


adolescent
line @1 greet : Welcome. I've saved the dry forward step. | Stand by the hem of my imagined awning.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : A new visitor may claim my dry forward corner. | Hello. There is comfortable room for your step.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The light lays out my future counter rather neatly. | First light measures the width without asking a fee.
line @1 greet.return : Hello in return. I was just finishing the fourth corner. | I've set my little measure down to listen.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You know which step belongs to the buyer. | My familiar partner in the dry corner again.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Evening. The night makes a generous ceiling. | There's a quiet measure left before I put my plan away.
line @1 again.open : Back to the measure where we last left it. | The little market has scarcely shifted in your absence.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come stand under the awning I haven't bought yet! | The empty corner could use your dancing feet!
line @1 farewell : A dry dancing step wherever your errands lead. | May your way home finish in good time.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll mind the unoccupied square of floor. | Go while you can enjoy a free stretch of pavement.
line @1 react.news : Give the account a little floor of its own. | I'll hear the whole measure without rushing your step.
line @1 react.news.new : That wasn't on my plan of the morning. | Another unfamiliar figure in my market row.
line @1 react.news.known : I remember the same turn in the earlier account. | We've danced past that particular notice before.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That final step appears to hang in open air. | I'd want the middle of the figure made clearer first.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : Here is the sheltered side while the loss feels close. | I can leave my little plans folded and hear your sorrow.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Excellent. That calls for a turn round the whole dry floor. | Happy news will fit a much longer measure.
line @1 ask.how : Has today's going been pleasant underfoot? | Has anything given your morning a lighter step?
line @1 answer.how : Low in spirits, fairly steady in my measure. | All right. I still see the bright corner under the clouds.
line @1 decline : I haven't quite the breadth of spare time that would need. | My promised piece of floor is full today.
line @1 accept_decline : Then I'll shift the measure off your side. | We can leave your share entirely unclaimed.
line @1 preclose : I should return to the unmeasured corner. | Time I set the next copper carefully aside.
line @1 accept_preclose : Dance the remaining figure just as you please. | My stall has plenty of patience between our meetings.
line @1 thank : You gave my plan another inch of shelter. Thank you. | That kindness left me room for a real step forward.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was a place I'd already measured for a second wolf. | One little step won't wear out the imaginary floor.
line @1 sympathise : Come under the broad part while the weather feels cruel. | Your grief has no performance to give here.
line @1 reassure : We need only cross to the sheltered edge of this figure. | There's space to turn gently instead of finishing in a rush.
line @1 ack : Yes. That fits my four corners quite comfortably. | I see how your step meets mine.
line @1 give.advice : Price enough cloth to cover the waiting visitor too. | Keep your feet outside the swing of a loaded basket.
scene planstep
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I have a market awning four dance steps across. At present the steps are the part I own.
b : Which is paid for next? | Why start with steps?
a : The first handspan of cloth, copper by copper. Cloth doesn't care how fine my house looks. | Because I can measure where a customer should stand before I have money for a single post.

scene rainend
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I watch the rain until the pauses between drops give me time for one small turning figure.
b : Can you actually stop it? | Why wait for pauses?
a : I could easily afford an enormous awning if I could command the weather. I can only watch. | The sound of a shoe landing in a clear moment is a little more distinct. I like giving the dance its proper ending.

scene study
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : During lessons I practise drawing a straight stall front and dividing the spaces for the baskets.
b : Does that count as arithmetic? | Where would you keep a book?
a : When each basket has a cost and a width, very emphatically. My sums have acquired a roof. | Above the table with enough cover to read prices in a downpour.

scene loft
when topic=home self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From the Heights a whole jumble of awnings looks like patches on a single neat blanket.
b : Does the blanket have holes? | Would you trade from up here?
a : Where the streets go through, yes. It's easy to overlook the buyers getting wet in those handsome gaps. | My plan belongs in the Commons, where one can actually stand beside the market traffic.

scene dance
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dance taught me the difference between room to stand and room to turn carrying something.
b : What did you carry? | Is a turn much wider?
a : My sleeve first, then an empty basket. An ordinary errand can have rather generous elbows. | The basket thinks so. I'd rather learn it with a dance figure than with a customer's breakfast.

scene maproad
when topic=travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My old map places a market road where no reasonable dance step could reach it.
b : Why use that sheet? | What does a dance prove?
a : The mistaken road leaves just enough clear paper for my own little row. | Merely my own turning width. The best proof of a road is still going there with a basket.

scene herring
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like herring folded small enough to eat between dances. It leaves me a free hand for the next turn.
b : Does the brine drip? | Would you sell herring?
a : With a clean scrap of bread beneath, very little. I prefer the flavour on the food to the flavour on my cuff. | I'd consider it if I could keep a shelf for wrappings quite separate from a shelf for money.

scene frostmorning
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A frosty morning draws my four steps on the sill before I've really begun the day.
b : With your hand? | Do they stay all day?
a : One finger. I can place the entire market in a strip no wider than my wrist. | Only till the sun comes round. A short tenancy but a remarkably modest rent.

scene saltgap
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Salt wind finds the gap where I have imagined the awning's side. I may have to dance myself another foot of cloth.
b : Will that cost more? | Does your counter have to face that way?
a : Yes. I'll put a shuttle's width aside slowly. I'd like anybody standing there to taste the food rather than the wind. | Sometimes, but a stall has neighbours. I can't rotate the entire market to suit my herring.

scene smokeeye
when topic=health self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave space for a sidestep out of any smoke drifting into my space by the front hem.
b : Won't some other wolf get it? | Why not a full screen?
a : That's why I examine how the entire row sits. My clean breath shouldn't cost a neighbour a dirty one. | A screen that keeps smoke out might keep the smoke in as well. I'd like the air to have its own passage.

scene motherplan
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.mother# the first space under my awning before putting a price on anything.
b : Why the first place? | What if rain starts?
a : It would make the coppers I've saved feel more solid to see a dear face under the cloth my money bought. | All the better for showing what those little savings really paid for.

scene quietpurse
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the first copper for the awning aside before planning all the colours I'd like it to have.
b : Which colour would you choose? | Are the savings necessary?
a : Something pale underneath so I can read prices, and a cheerful colour facing the street. | I want a stall I have saved for myself. I should know how a day of slow sales feels.

story wetmeasure [topic=weather|memories]
  : I measured an awning by chalking my feet round the first dry patch I found. Stood back and admired a very long narrow plan.
  : The patch was under the dry outline of my own shoulders after a sprinkling shower. I had designed a stall almost exactly my width.
  b : Where did the buyer go?
  : On the next drawing. I took four honest measures with a basket instead of trusting a flattering patch of stone.

story dancingfish [topic=food|memories]
  : I packed two wrapped herring bites together to practise changing my basket hand at each turn. A tidy figure from the outside.
  : At the last turn both parcels were in the same hand, and I was politely offering an empty basket to the wall.
  b : Did either herring survive the dance?
  : We had a very quiet supper while I considered a less ambitious piece of choreography.

story mapcloth [topic=travel|memories]
  : A market road on my old map once looked as if it continued straight through a blue square. I held the sheet up to the window.
  : The road was a crease continuing through the marked square. No roadmaker had been quite so unreasonable.
  b : Did that ruin the layout?
  : Improved it. I could use the entire square for imaginary stalls and still fold the map properly when the rain came.

rule @awning
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four clear turns and a generous strip for the front. | The saved copper goes toward that bit of the roof.

rule @dance
when concept=bark self.likes=dancing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Basket changes hands under the driest section of canvas. | Small turn by the buyer's end, then home.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One clear interval, then the long patter again. | Rain along the hem has its own last measure.

rule @herring
when concept=bark self.likes=pickled_herring
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A little bread under the sharp fold, please. | A dry wrapper for the hand that carries the herring.

dlg @1 resident.hub : You can stand on the customer's side of my imagined awning. I always measure enough room there.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, the forward step is just where we left it.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Night has made my market plan almost all quiet corners. There's still one free.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : The full width of my counter can stand between us while we speak.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My lessons find themselves applied to shop cloth, steps and the cost of a copper's worth of each.
dlg @2 resident.job : I care for work that gives the next arrival a comfortable place to stand.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Find a pleasant measure where the awnings cover your walk.
graft resident.hub
choice Can I take a turn under your imagined awning? -> drydance
node drydance
say Take one pace forward with an imaginary basket. Turn it to your other hand. If it stays clear of my elbow and of the rain, we have a reasonable width.
free
choice What happens if our baskets meet? -> widercloth
choice I can see the dry front edge. -> hub
node widercloth
say I measure the next copper's worth of cloth. My aim is a market where nobody needs an instructed dance partner simply to buy a herring in comfort.
choice We could try the turn again. -> hub
choice I'll bring a smaller basket. -> bye
